  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strict: all incidents reported within 48h, records kept, reporting even when cause uncertain, customer notice within 5 days. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% review threshold but does not mandate sales stop above 5%, and gives customers individual failure rates without public publication. S3 requires new-unit shut-off from 24 months and retrofit within six years. S4 requires built-in suppression from 36 months. S5 uses an 8/100k review trigger but leaves recall to regulator discretion, with prompt customer notices."
